well a high profile visit from the u.s  agriculture secretary's office  here in southern nevada officials are  checking out how summer feeding programs  are working out in local schools hector  mejia reports  hey there well secretary vilsack is  making stops at a number of communities  across the country today it was  henderson's turn here at mcdonald  elementary where that tour happened  during lunch service  and we've learned one in four students  here in clark county are food insecure  meaning  they don't often know where their next  meal will come from  u.s agriculture secretary tom vilsack  said the american rescue plan  created a summer feeding program but  it's only for a year and there's now  push to make it a permanent program  so today he met with governor steve  sisilak along with u.s congresswoman  susie lee  they went over the biden  administration's goal to promote healthy  eating  and how the american family's plan will  help achieve that goal  it is an issue of food security it is  also an issue of nutrition  and what we saw today here at mcdonald's  school  is a commitment to both making sure that  youngsters are fed even during a  pandemic  millions of meals but also making sure  that they're fed well  the carrots the apple slices  good snacks quality snacks for  youngsters here in clark county as many  as three out of four students  qualify for free or reduced lunches and  the secretary also talked about the  president's  infrastructure plan and how they're  working to pass a bipartisan package  to get the economy moving faster we are  in henderson this afternoon hector mejia  8 news now
 

